Subject: [PATCH] scsi: ufs: ufs-qcom: skip enabling lane clocks if already enabled

ufs_qcom_init_lane_clks() acquires all controller clocks via
devm_clk_bulk_get_all() into host->clks (including GCC AXI/AHB/ICE/UniPro
clocks and TCSR ref_clk on SM8550).  While ufs_qcom_disable_lane_clks()
guards clk_bulk_disable_unprepare() with if (!host->is_lane_clks_enabled),
ufs_qcom_enable_lane_clks() lacked the symmetric early return when
host->is_lane_clks_enabled is already true.

On every runtime resume from HIBERN8 (rpm_lvl=3), ufshcd_runtime_resume()
invokes ufs_qcom_setup_clocks(on=true, PRE_CHANGE) ->
ufs_qcom_enable_lane_clks(), and immediately afterward
ufshcd_wl_runtime_resume() invokes ufs_qcom_resume() ->
ufs_qcom_enable_lane_clks() a second time.  Likewise, system resume from
link-off calls ufs_qcom_enable_lane_clks() in both ufs_qcom_resume() and
ufs_qcom_hce_enable_notify(PRE_CHANGE).  Because the matching disable only
decrements the refcount once, every resume permanently leaks +1 on all 9
UFS clocks (including tcsr_ufs_pad_clkref_en -> bi_tcxo and gcc_gpll0),
preventing XO/CXSD/AOSD/DDR collapse during PM_SUSPEND_MEM.

Return 0 early in ufs_qcom_enable_lane_clks() when host->is_lane_clks_enabled
is already true, matching ufs_qcom_disable_lane_clks().

---
--- a/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c
@@ -356,6 +356,9 @@ static int ufs_qcom_enable_lane_clks(struct ufs_qcom_host *host)
 {
 	int err;
 
+	if (host->is_lane_clks_enabled)
+		return 0;
+
 	err = clk_bulk_prepare_enable(host->num_clks, host->clks);
 	if (err)
 		return err;
